From c7636af72db7a4c649914ff3fe9bb67b184a16d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wu Zhipeng <zepwu@foxmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 11:35:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] platform/x86: panasonic-laptop: add platform_profile quirk
 for CF-SV1-2

Add a platform_profile quirk for the Panasonic CF-SV1-2 (Let's Note,
Tiger Lake), verified on hardware under Linux with BIOS V2.00L23; the
later V2.00L24 update leaves every firmware table byte-identical.  The
firmware exposes the same fan and TDP policy controls as CF-SR4 and the
boolean mapping is identical (COOL active+locked, QUIET passive+locked,
PERFORMANCE active+unlocked), so the model reuses quirk_cf_sr4 and only
adds a DMI entry; the remaining fan/TDP combination is reported as
CUSTOM by get().

Measured on the unit under EPP=performance (turbo on, no userspace fan
governor; 3 interleaved rounds x 4 EC states, 60 s sysbench cpu --threads=8
with 1 Hz RAPL sampling), the TDP toggle is the power lever and the fan
toggle a temperature lever: active+locked sustains 9.96 W at 50 C,
quiet+locked 9.95 W at 60 C, active+unlocked 26.32 W at 84 C and
quiet+unlocked 25.63 W at 88 C.  Locking the TDP therefore holds the
package at about 10 W against about 26 W unlocked, while the fan curve
moves the peak temperature by about 10 C when locked and 4 C when
unlocked, at essentially equal package power.

Model-specific behaviour is noted here because it does not generalise
across models: the SEFM curve-byte values are swapped against CF-SR4
(CF-SV1: 0x00 cool / 0x05 quiet / 0x02 in S0i3), EPLE/SEPL select an IETM
table PL rather than a fixed TDP cap, _FST[1] is a fan setpoint and not
RPM, a nonzero TFN1._FSL override masks a profile change until it is
released, and the EC comes up at boot with CEFM=0 / EPLE=1
(active + locked / COOL).

Signed-off-by: Wu Zhipeng <zepwu@foxmail.com>
---
Starting point against RFC v3, not for direct merge.  Per Ilpo's
2026-10-16 review this reuses the existing quirk_cf_sr4 struct and only
adds a DMI entry instead of declaring a duplicate struct.  The post-image
index line is omitted on purpose; it will be regenerated when the series
is rebased onto v4.
---
 drivers/platform/x86/panasonic-laptop.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/platform/x86/panasonic-laptop.c b/drivers/platform/x86/panasonic-laptop.c
--- a/drivers/platform/x86/panasonic-laptop.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/x86/panasonic-laptop.c
@@ -355,6 +355,14 @@ static const struct dmi_system_id pcc_profile_quirks[] = {
 		},
 		.driver_data = &quirk_cf_sr4,
 	},
+	{
+		.ident = "Panasonic Corporation CFSV1-2",
+		.matches = {
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_SYS_VENDOR, "Panasonic Corporation"),
+			DMI_MATCH(DMI_PRODUCT_NAME, "CFSV1-2"),
+		},
+		.driver_data = &quirk_cf_sr4,
+	},
 	{
 		.ident = "Panasonic Corporation CFQV9-1",
 		.matches = {
-- 
